# "is not an object" and "is not a function" are the engine's errors, worded by the engine. Where it quotes the source of the expression that failed, a compiled frame
# has no source: the engine quotes the name of the member, which the place that fails holds anyway: the null check of a typed read and of a typed store, a read and a store by name,
# and a call of what is never an object, in the middle of a function and as its last act.
